---

<Layout title="Light and Optics">

    <div slot="navtree">
        <ul class='list-group list-group-flush py-0'> 
            <li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsection' href='#matter'>Light and Matter</a>
                <ul class='list-group list-group-flush py-0'> 
                    <li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsubsection' href='#reflection'>Reflection</a></li> 
					<li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsubsection' href='#refraction'>Refraction</a></li>
					<li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsubsection' href='#geometry'>Useful Geometry</a></li>					
					
                </ul>
            </li>
            <li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsection' href='#int-dif'>Interference and Diffraction</a>
			<ul class='list-group list-group-flush py-0'> 
                   <li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsubsection' href='#double'>Double Slit Interference</a></li>
				   <li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsubsection' href='#single'>Single Slit Diffraction</a></li>
					<li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsubsection' href='#circular'>Circular Aperture Diffraction</a></li>
<li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsubsection' href='#small'>Small Angle Approximations</a></li>					
                </ul></li>
            <li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsection' href='#geo-opt'>Geometric Optics</a><ul class='list-group list-group-flush py-0'> 
				<li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsubsection' href='#double'>Mirror and Lens Equations</a></li>
				   <li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsubsection' href='#single'>Telescope Magnification</a></li>
					<li class='list-group-item py-0'><a class='text-decoration-none subsubsection' href='#circular'>Compound Microscope Magnification</a></li>
        </ul>
		</li>
    </div>



<Section id="main-section" title="Light and Optics">
        <p>
            This page provides a key to interpreting symbols and units in Introductory Electricity & Magnetism, and provides values of constants in SI units.
        </p>
        

        
    </Section>

<SubSection id="matter" title="Light and Matter">

<SubSubSection id="reflection" title="Reflection">
<DisplayEquation equation="\\theta_{incident}=\\theta_{reflected}" title="Light reflects off a surface at an angle equal to its incident angle (Law of reflection):" background="True" />
</SubSubSection>

<SubSubSection id="refraction" title="Refraction">
	
<DisplayEquation equation="v=\\frac{c}{n}" title="The speed of an EM wave changes when it travels through matter. The index of refraction n tells us how much:" background="True" />	

<DisplayEquation equation="n_1\\sin\\theta_1=n_2\\sin\\theta_2" title="EM waves bend when they change medium ('Snell's Law'):" background="True" />

<DisplayEquation equation="\\sin\\theta_c=\\frac{n_2}{n_1}" title="Total internal reflection happens at the critical angle:" background="True" />
            
    
</SubSubSection>

<SubSubSection id="geometry" title="Useful Geometry">
<p>The sum of all angles in a triangle is 180 deg.<p>
<p>The sum of all angles in a quadrilateral is 360 deg.</p>
<p>The sum of all angles that make a line is 180 deg.</p>
<p>Something about parallel lines and angles</p>
<p>Something about similar triangles</p>
</SubSubSection>

</SubSection>	    
</Layout>
